From: Jörg Krause <jkrause@posteo.de>
Subject: [PATCH] examples/testd.c: include <unistd.h> instead of <sys/unistd.h>

As the C POSIX library recommends include the <unistd.h> instead of
<sys/unistd.h>. This removes an error when building libdaemon against
the musl C library.

Carried from the cports guidance tree (cports/main/libdaemon/patches/
unistd.patch); Saphira is musl-only so the non-portable header can
never resolve here.
--- a/examples/testd.c
+++ b/examples/testd.c
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 #include <string.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <sys/time.h>
-#include <sys/unistd.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 #include <sys/select.h>

 #include <libdaemon/dfork.h>
